<https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/live/job/arbeitnow-associate-director-head-of-high-throughput-lab-cambridge-427787> a prov:Entity,
        schema:JobPosting ;
    dcterms:source <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/source/arbeitnow> ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-25T04:44:23+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/flagshippioneeringinc/associate-director-head-of-high-throughput-lab-cambridge-427787> ;
    kgjobs:active true ;
    kgjobs:canonicalFingerprint "6b7eea6427c1c3e040e42f72197ee82784565f685cc4cf92d14658a865d126f4" ;
    kgjobs:classification "not_match" ;
    kgjobs:firstSeenAt "2026-08-25T01:35:30+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:lastSeenAt "2026-08-25T04:44:23+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "associate-director-head-of-high-throughput-lab-cambridge-427787" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-24"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "<p><strong>Position Summary:</strong></p> <p>Quotient is seeking an experienced Associate Director, Head of High Throughput Laboratory to lead and continuously develop the high-throughput laboratory supporting our somatic genomics platform.&nbsp;This is a pivotal leadership role within a rapidly growing biotechnology company, responsible for delivering high-quality, reproducible multi-omic data across Quotient's disease portfolio. Reporting to the Head of Research Strategy &amp; Operations, the incumbent will lead multidisciplinary teams spanning histology, flow cytometry, molecular biology and scientific management, ensuring laboratory delivery remains aligned with research priorities while building a high-performing, scalable function.&nbsp;Working in close partnership with scientific leadership, assay development, automation and research project management, you will translate research priorities into efficient laboratory execution, embedding operational excellence, scientific quality and continuous improvement.</p> <p><strong>Responsibilities:&nbsp;</strong></p> <ul> <li>Lead, develop and inspire a multidisciplinary team of Scientific Managers, Subject Matter Experts and Research Associates, fostering a high-performing, collaborative and accountable culture</li> <li>Translate company strategy and portfolio priorities into clear laboratory delivery plans, ensuring the High Throughput Laboratory consistently delivers high-quality, reproducible scientific data safely, efficiently and to agreed project milestones while maintaining the highest standards of health and safety, regulatory compliance and data integrity</li> <li>Provide operational leadership across Histology, Flow Cytometry, Molecular Biology and Scientific Sample Management, ensuring laboratory capacity, capability and resource planning support both current and future portfolio demands</li> <li>Partner closely with Research Project Management, Scientific Leadership, Assay Development and Automation to align laboratory execution with integrated project plans, operational priorities and future platform requirements</li> <li>Develop, implement and continuously improve scalable laboratory systems, workflows and operational best practices that increase laboratory quality, efficiency, throughput and reproducibility</li> <li>Develop and monitor laboratory performance metrics and KPIs, using data to drive operational performance, capacity planning and continuous improvement across the High Throughput Laboratory</li> <li>Identify opportunities for strategic investment in laboratory infrastructure, equipment, staffing and technology to ensure laboratory capability evolves alongside Quotient's research portfolio</li> <li>Develop organisational capability through succession planning, workforce development, coaching and creation of clear career pathways, ensuring Scientific Managers and Subject Matter Experts continue to grow as future organisational leaders</li> <li>Build strong collaborative relationships across Research, Data Science and AI, Assay Development, Laboratory Operations, Project Management and external partners, representing the High Throughput Laboratory in organisational planning, governance and strategic discussions</li> <li>Foster a culture of continuous improvement and psychological safety, empowering teams to challenge constructively, embrace innovation and continuously improve the way science is delivered</li> </ul> <p><strong>Qualifications:</strong></p> <p><u>Essential</u></p> <ul> <li>MSc or PhD in Biology or a related scientific discipline with significant post-academic biotechnology experience</li> <li>Significant experience leading and developing multidisciplinary laboratory teams</li> <li>Proven experience operating and scaling high-throughput laboratory environments</li> <li>Strong understanding of genomics and multi-omics workflows and high-throughput laboratory operations</li> <li>Demonstrated success implementing operational improvements that increase quality, efficiency and scalability</li> <li>Experience balancing day-to-day laboratory delivery with long-term capability development</li> <li>Excellent understanding of laboratory health &amp; safety, quality systems and regulatory compliance</li> <li>Outstanding people leadership, coaching and organisational development skills</li> </ul> <p><u>Desirable</u></p> <ul> <li>Experience supporting genomics-based drug target identification and early discovery research</li> <li>Experience working collaboratively with laboratory automation teams to implement workflow improvements and new technologies</li> <li>Experience working within rapidly scaling biotechnology organisations</li> <li>Experience supporting matrix organisations delivering multiple concurrent research programs</li> <li>Experience embedding operational excellence methodologies into working teams</li> </ul> <p><strong>Values and Behaviors:</strong></p> <ul> <li>Encourage respectful disagreement and cultivate open-minded, ego-free interactions to continuously push each other towards excellence</li> <li>Seek out diverse perspectives; practice active listening and genuine curiosity to ensure all contributions are valued, regardless of source</li> <li>Recognize the impact of your behavior, language and attitudes, and strive for balanced, meaningful exchanges that enhance mutual growth and understanding in all interactions</li> <li>Use a company-first mindset to guide decision-making; prioritize team over individual success</li> <li>Take calculated risks and challenge convention in the quest for exceptional outcomes</li> </ul> <p><strong>About Quotient:</strong></p> <p>Quotient Therapeutics is a privately-held, early stage company developing breakthrough medicines informed by natural somatic genetic diversity present in patients. Through our work in somatic genomics, we are forging a new status quo for biopharma research and development across a broad pipeline of internal and partnered programs.&nbsp;</p> <p>The company was founded by Flagship Pioneering, an innovative enterprise that conceives, creates, resources, and grows first-in-category life sciences companies. Flagship Pioneering has created over 100 groundbreaking companies over the past twenty years, all of which are pioneering novel and proprietary biological, industrial, and engineering approaches to solve major needs in human health and sustainability. These companies include Moderna (MRNA), Generate Biomedicines, Sana Biotechnology (SANA), Tessera Therapeutics, Evelo Biosciences (EVLO), Indigo Agriculture, Seres Therapeutics (MCRB), and Syros Pharmaceuticals (SYRS).</p><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><p>&nbsp;</p> <p style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Privacy Notice for Applicants:&nbsp;</strong>When you apply for a role at Flagship Pioneering or one of its portfolio companies, we collect and use personal information you provide (such as your name, contact details, work history, and application materials) to evaluate your application, communicate with you, and comply with legal obligations. Your application data is processed through Greenhouse, our applicant tracking system, and may also be reviewed using AI-assisted screening tools. We do not sell your personal information. California residents have rights under the CCPA/CPRA including to know, delete, and opt out of the sharing of their personal information. If you are located in the EU or UK, we process your data under GDPR and you have rights to access, rectify, and erase your data. To exercise your rights or for questions, contact ----- Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:hiringOrganization kgjd:employer-flagshippioneeringinc ;
    schema:identifier "arbeitnow-associate-director-head-of-high-throughput-lab-cambridge-427787" ;
    schema:jobLocation [ a schema:Place ;
            schema:name "Cambridge" ] ;
    schema:title "Associate Director, Head of High Throughput Lab" ;
    schema:url <https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/flagshippioneeringinc/associate-director-head-of-high-throughput-lab-cambridge-427787> .

<https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/live/job/arbeitnow-associate-partner-ai-data-life-sciences-berlin-62207> a prov:Entity,
        schema:JobPosting ;
    dcterms:source <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/source/arbeitnow> ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-25T04:44:23+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/visium/associate-partner-ai-data-life-sciences-berlin-62207> ;
    kgjobs:active true ;
    kgjobs:canonicalFingerprint "5475b1641d4100d8e77fe57ae4d2f9eb92af53e9f08f60e16746c056cb5f75b6" ;
    kgjobs:classification "not_match" ;
    kgjobs:firstSeenAt "2026-08-25T01:35:30+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:lastSeenAt "2026-08-25T04:44:23+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "associate-partner-ai-data-life-sciences-berlin-62207" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-24"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Visium combines strategy, frontier AI, and deep regulated-industry expertise to build and deploy AI-native systems that reinvent how businesses operate - unlocking the value of AI at scale. We're not a strategy firm that ships slide decks and walks away. Not a tech consultancy that builds what won't get adopted. Not a product company chasing problems it doesn't understand. We're all three at once: strategy, deep technical and integration expertise, and product, working as one. That combination is our flywheel. Consulting keeps us close to the hardest real-world problems. Products let us solve them at scale. Every engagement sharpens our products; every deployment makes the next engagement faster, deeper, and more certain. We're obsessed with outcomes. While 95% of enterprise AI pilots never reach production, Visium is built to be the 5% delivering productised AI that compounds in value, not point solutions that deliver marginal gains. We are AI-native, not AI-adjacent. We don't bolt AI onto broken workflows; we redesign them with AI at the core. Role At Visium, you'll have the opportunity to take on an entrepreneurial role, contributing to the organization’s growth and finding innovative ways to create meaningful impact for clients. Your mission will involve advising C-Level executives on their AI & Data strategies and guiding large-scale digital transformations. You’ll act as a trusted advisor and a key source of strategic insight, overseeing and nurturing long-term client relationships while ensuring the highest quality of delivery. As an Associate Partner you will be responsible for: Creating new business opportunities and expanding existing ones. Rely on your extensive network and collaborate with our business development team to create new business opportunities in LifeScience. Engage with our client’s C-level stakeholders to understand their Data and AI related challenges, developing solutions and support them in implementing and scaling them in a sustainable way. Lead and collaborate effectively within large cross-functional teams to review and analyze client requirements or challenges and provide leadership and direction to elevate our delivery capabilities. Lead engagement teams in developing logical and insightful analyses; innovative & effective recommendations and high-quality deliverables. Depending on your previous experiences and appetite to grow, you will play an active role in practice development. Requirements What we are looking for Director, Associate Partner/Partner level (or equivalent title) experience at a consulting firm. Data Science background and specialization across LifeScience & Healthcare are required. Proven track record of developing new client relationships and generating business development opportunities that leads to successful client engagements. Demonstrated ability with the management of a portfolio of healthcare clients generating 7 figures in revenues in a consulting-like industry. Experience leading cross-functional teams and in-depth knowledge/defined involvement in helping frame, design and implement and scale solutions for challenging business situations. Exceptional intellectual and analytical curiosity, a creative visionary who can drive innovation. Ability to communicate complex ideas effectively – both verbally and in writing – in English. French and/or German are considered a plus. Benefits Benefits What we offer A competitive compensation package A yearly education budget to steep your learning curve A yearly sport budget because a fit body leads to a fit mind A flexible working culture because your work-life balance matters to us A position that enables you to have an impact on 1’000s of people, and the whole company's growth. An international, knowledgeable, and passionate team with a strong collaborative mindset Check our LinkedIn and website to learn more about us & don’t hesitate to contact us if you have any questions. Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Full time" ;
