    schema:description "At Ubitium, we believe the best engineering happens when people with different perspectives tackle hard problems together. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds and experiences. What matters most is curiosity, skill, and the drive to build technology that improves the world. If that resonates with you, we’d love to hear from you. Our team members come from some of the best universities in the world and left some of the largest tech companies to build something truly remarkable. Tasks We are looking for a Compiler Engineer who will develop new heuristics for a place-and-route tool and take over its overall maintenance and integration. Focus areas include, but are not limited to: Design and implementation of heuristics based on feedback from our application engineers; taking over the ongoing maintenance and improvement of the tool; integration of an externally developed optimal solver. Requirements Prospective team members require strong C++ skills and a solid grounding in graph algorithms and optimisation; experience with Python or similar scripting languages; interest in or exposure to EDA / place-and-route, CGRA, FPGA, or compiler back-end mapping. Familiarity with ILP solvers is a plus. Master’s degree (or equivalent experience) and first relevant experience (internships, projects) welcome. Relocation required. Currently 4 days on-site, 1 day remote. Policy may change. Benefits Competitive salary plus stock options 30+ days of paid vacation Relocation support Full German social security and universal healthcare A modern office Free snacks, coffee, and drinks Work with people who actually know their stuff – computer architects, hardware nerds, and engineers who love tough problems. A culture where new ideas matter, but so does respect and collaboration. Space to grow: pick up new skills, dig into areas that interest you, and shape your own path. Get hands-on with real implementations of AI and signal processing – not just slides or buzzwords. An inclusive team where different perspectives are valued and everyone contributes. We are constantly looking for talent. We recruit through multiple channels – friends & colleagues, universities and professors we know, recruiters, conventions, e-mails and LinkedIn. Join us today. Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
