    schema:description "Your Responsibilities The University of Europe is seeking a freelance math instructor with teaching experience to teach Foundation Mathematics in our Hamburg location. The ideal candidate will possess the following qualifications: Requirements: · Proven teaching experience in Mathematics. · Experience teaching international groups. · Proficiency in English, with the ability to teach basic mathematical concepts in English. Teaching Responsibilities: · Instruct Foundation Mathematics courses, focusing on fundamental concepts such as functions, systems of equations, matrices, logic, and probability. · Equip students with the mathematical skills necessary for research and scientific reasoning in their university studies. · Conduct formative tests and a final exam to assess students’ progress. · Attendance tracking · Collaboration with the program management team · Prepare Foundation students for the Bachelor programme and the admission exam. Semester Workload: · 3 hours of instruction per week (SWS). Location: Hamburg Payrate: 40€ per hour If you meet the above criteria and are passionate about teaching mathematics to a diverse, international student body, we encourage you to apply. Please send your CV and a cover letter detailing your teaching experience and approach to career foundations <Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
