    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "gcp-and-ai-instructor-london-409608" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-24"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "At Jellyfish, we believe in the power of diverse perspectives and inclusive collaboration. We welcome individuals who excel in collaborative, varied teams and value the unique contributions that each person brings to the table. Jellyfish is a global digital marketing agency, a unique fusion of tech enthusiasts, creative minds, and media and data experts all united to empower our clients along their digital journey. Our commitment to embracing diverse perspectives fuels our innovation and strategies that challenge the status quo, reinvent media activation, and craft influential stories for our global clients and their customers. Join us in shaping a future where business growth and personal fulfilment go hand in hand. Job Description We are looking for GCP and AI Instructors to join our team of instructors. This role offers flexible, hybrid working arrangements. As part of our award-winning team, you will help support our customers and deliver high-quality instruction globally to some of the world’s largest brands. We require an experienced Cloud professional with a passion for teaching. It may be that you are already a seasoned GCP instructor, or that you have a talent for sharing knowledge but are not yet a certified instructor. Any applicant must be extremely experienced with the creation of solutions using GCP technologies. Instructors could be asked to teach a range of topics from the comprehensive Google Cloud certification paths. Therefore, holding a wide range of certifications is essential. Please include detailed information on which certifications you currently hold upon application. Beyond general cloud infrastructure, a strong understanding of AI-related topics is absolutely essential. You will lead courses across Gemini Enterprise, Gemini Enterprise Agent PlatformI, and GenAI architecture. If you have a passion for sharing knowledge, developing AI training curriculums, and presenting to enterprise clients, this is the perfect role for you. Please note this will be a 12-month fixed-term contractual position Your primary responsibilities will include: Deliver virtual classroom sessions globally. Flexibility is paramount; this is not a strict 9-5 role. Instruct courses covering any topics from the Google Cloud certification paths, adapting to varying client needs. Provide occasional face-to-face training to clients in your region, with potential opportunities for international travel to deliver overseas courses. Google Cloud AI Curriculum Delivery: whilst not extensive, there may be some opportunity to help develop custom courseware and materials. Take responsibility for keeping pace with the rapidly evolving GCP technology landscape, particularly in AI. Maintain and grow your range of current valid GCP certifications. Qualifications What you’ll need: Essential Certifications: A wide range of Google Cloud certifications is required to cover the diverse certification paths. (Please detail which you hold upon application). A minimum of 5 years’ experience with Cloud Technologies. Strong understanding of AI-related topics. Comfortable presenting and delivering multiple-day-long training sessions both in the classroom and online. Comfortable in training enterprise-level clients on how to develop or diversify their current skill set. Clear communication of processes, strategies, and general requirements to both internal and external stakeholders. Systems Operations experience, including deploying and managing applications, either on-premises or in a public cloud environment. Advantageous: Second languages. Understanding of competitors in the landscape Strong business awareness and ability to talk to leadership teams. Highly organised, with the ability to work on multiple projects at once. An excellent writer and communicator, comfortable speaking to advanced audiences, large groups, etc. Note: We emphasise skills, expertise and behavioural attributes over years of experience and traditional degrees. If you want to join our collaborative team, we invite you to apply today with your resume in English. Additional Information Join Jellyfish and experience a workplace where we prioritise your growth, celebrate your contributions, and empower you to tailor your work environment to suit your needs. 💰 Reward: You'll be eligible to join our discretionary annual bonus scheme. 💫 Custom Work Environment: Work remotely for up to 60% of your days and shape your day between 8am. and 6:30pm with flexible working hours. 📈 Growth, Your Way: Accumulate one paid day each month (2 hours per week) for self-development and access to Jellyfish Learn. 👪 Family Support: Enjoy 14 weeks of paid leave for primary caregivers and 4 weeks of paid leave for secondary caregivers. We also provide £1000 (or equivalent) towards courses for returning primary caregivers to support your transition back into work. Unfortunately, there has been an increase in fake recruiters impersonating Jellyfish and unlawfully using our brand name. If you are unsure if an email with a job offer you have received is genuinely from Jellyfish, or if you suspect any fraudulent activity, please report it to Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
