experienced and fluent in English for teaching and research purposes. You demonstrate significant publications. You possess research experience, ideally including the acquisition of funding. You will provide new innovative directions for research and teaching. Ideally, you are experienced in curriculum development and accreditation processes. Why us? A full-time employment contract, including 18 weekly semester teaching hours. A versatile, innovative and international work environment in cooperation with renowned partner universities and cooperation partners. The opportunity for progression within a dynamic, entrepreneurial university environment. Senior responsibilities and creative freedom. The opportunity for personal and professional development. Interested? If you are interested in joining us, we look forward to receiving your detailed online application indicating the area for which you would like to be considered. Please include: CV Your degree certificates Research and teaching statement including list of five relevant publications Work certificates/professional references Your earliest possible start date. Please submit your application by 30.09.2026 to be considered. Gisma is an equal opportunity employer. As such, we explicitly encourage applications from underrepresented groups, in particular disabled persons who meet the criteria will be given preference. Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
