    schema:datePosted "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Who We Are We build the intelligence that lets robots sense, reason, and act in the real world—moving beyond the lab and into everyday industrial settings like warehouses and factories. Our technology closes the automation gaps that traditional systems can't solve. We are on a mission to redefine how physical work gets done, and we're looking for curious, bold thinkers to help shape the future of robotics with us. Overview We are looking for a motivated and hands-on intern to join our team and take part in testing and demonstration of our AI robotics products. In this role, you will work closely with our engineering and product teams to validate new features, help maintain demo environments, and ensure our product showcases run smoothly for customers and stakeholders. This is a great opportunity to gain real-world experience at the intersection of robotics, AI, and product development. Your Responsibilities Testing Assist with testing new features as they are developed and integrated into our robotics systems. Execute test cases, document results, and report bugs or unexpected behavior to the engineering team. Help identify edge cases and contribute to improving test coverage across hardware and software components. Participate in regression testing efforts before product releases. Demo Help set up and maintain in-house demo stations, ensuring all hardware and software components are functioning correctly. Assist with preparing, running, and validating product and customer demos. Coordinate with internal teams to ensure demos reflect the latest product capabilities. Troubleshoot and resolve issues with demo setups in a timely manner. Qualifications Education and Experience Currently pursuing or recently completed a Bachelor's or Master's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Robotics, Mechatronics, or a related technical field. Prior internship or project experience in testing, robotics, or a technical product environment is a plus. Skills Basic understanding of software testing concepts and methodologies. Comfort working with Linux-based systems and command-line tools. Familiarity with Python or another scripting language. Strong attention to detail and a methodical approach to problem-solving. Good communication skills and the ability to work collaboratively in a team. Hands-on attitude and willingness to work with both hardware and software. Familiarity with robotics concepts, ROS, and robotic manipulators. Additional Skills / Nice to Have Experience with Docker or containerized environments. Familiarity with robotics systems, sensors, or industrial automation. Knowledge of German is a plus. Our Interview Plan Application Recruiter screen: A conversation to learn about your background, interests, and availability. Technical screen: A deeper look into your skills, problem-solving approach, and technical fit for this role. Final round: Meet the team leadership, discuss the role in more detail, and get a clear feel for the working environment. What We Offer Wellpass (gym membership) Flexible working hours Option to work from home when needed A motivated team and an open corporate culture Hands-on experience with cutting-edge AI robotics technology Mentorship and learning opportunities within a fast-paced startup Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
